<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Honoré II, Prince of Monaco</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1597–1662</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Honoré II was the first ruler of Monaco to style himself prince, from 1612. By the Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peronne">Péronne</a> of 1641 he placed Monaco under French protection and expelled its Spanish garrison, receiving the duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valentinois">Valentinois</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in return. He rebuilt the Prince's Palace and assembled a large collection of paintings.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/honore-ii-prince-of-monaco.jpg" alt="Honoré II, Prince of Monaco" width="320" height="399" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Philippe de Champaigne · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:HonoriusIIMonaco-1-.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
